{title: Perfect Peace}
{subtitle: Isaiah 26:3–4}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When the night [Eb]is long and restless and my [Bb/D]mind will not lie still
And my [Cm7]thoughts run like a river, running [Ab]anywhere they will
I [Eb]set my mind upon you like [Bb/D]a city on the stone
With [Cm7]salvation for its walls, [Ab]and I am not alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You keep in perfect [Bb]peace the mind that is stead[Cm7]fast
Because [Ab]it trusts in you
[Eb]Trust in the LORD forever
[Bb/D]For in the LORD, the LORD him[Cm7]self, is an everlasting [Ab]rock
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Ab] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Every [Eb]storm that shakes the windows, every [Bb/D]wave against the shore
[Cm7]Breaks upon a rock that stood a thou[Ab]sand years before
I will lean [Eb]my weight upon you, I will build [Bb/D]my house on you
You are [Cm7]steady in the morning and the [Ab]evening through
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You keep in perfect [Bb]peace the mind that is stead[Cm7]fast
Because it [Ab]trusts in you
[Eb]Trust in the LORD forever
[Bb/D]For in the LORD, the LORD him[Cm7]self, is an everlasting [Ab]rock
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Ab] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | ×2
| [Ab] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Perfect peace, [Bb]perfect peace [Cm7]
The [Ab]mind that is stead[Eb]fast
Because I trust in you
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb/D]Trust in the LORD forever
[Cm7]An everlasting [Ab]love
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Ab] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | ×2
